    "description": {
      "value": "<p>These reins are a heavy metal chain attached to a bridle set with glowing blue crystals. They have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can expend 1 charge to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplFindSteed0]{Find Steed} (level 5 version) from them.</p><p>The steed summoned with the reins is Invincible, the mount of Arthas: an Undead horse with mummified flesh, glowing blue eyes, and batlike wings. It has the Undead type, deals Necrotic damage with its Otherworldly Slam, and has the following Bonus Action.</p><p><strong>Ghostly Stride (Recharges after a Long Rest).</strong> The steed and its rider can move through other creatures and objects this turn as if they were Difficult Terrain. Both take 5 (1d10) Force damage if they end their turn inside an object.</p><p>Invincible is Neutral Evil and unshakably loyal to Arthas, the Lich King. Use the rules for conflict with sentient magic items in the Dungeon Master's Guide when its rider acts against its alignment or against the Lich King; Invincible can refuse the summons of the reins in such conflicts.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
